    {
      "id": "D4",
      "title": "At most two Send operations per plan, counted in order",
      "request": "New stateful rule for `Send`: operations are evaluated in the order the model proposed them. Keep a counter of accepted `Send` operations, starting at 0. For each `Send`, first apply the existing rules (recipient in `payees`); if it is refused by them it is left out and does NOT increment the counter. If it passes them and the counter is already 2, it is refused (left out); otherwise it is accepted and the counter is incremented. So at most 2 `Send` operations are executed per plan: the first two that pass the existing rules. Other kinds (`Schedule`, `Update`, `Retarget`, `Password`, `Profile`) are not counted and are not limited by this rule. Accepted operations execute in the proposed order.",
      "omission": "Incrementing the counter for every proposed Send, including those already refused because the recipient is not in payees, so a refused Send consumes one of the two slots.",
